WORKING - 12 DISC QUADRUPED - CONTROL IN TERMINAL 2

cd ~/soft_world
. ~/ros2_humble/install/local_setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
python3 scripts/control_quadraped_working.py --ros-args \
  -p front_left.phi_torque:=0.50 -p front_left.theta:=0.0 \
  -p front_right.phi_torque:=0.50 -p front_right.theta:=0.0 \
  -p rear_left.phi_torque:=0.50 -p rear_left.theta:=0.0 \
  -p rear_right.phi_torque:=0.50 -p rear_right.theta:=0.0

LEFT LEGS HAVE A NET 180-DEGREE LENGTH-AXIS ROTATION.
RIGHT LEGS HAVE A NET 360-DEGREE ROTATION AFTER THE ADDITIONAL 180-DEGREE TURN.
KEEP ALL NEUTRAL THETA COMMANDS AT 0.0 DEGREES.
USE POSITIVE TORQUE ON ALL FOUR LEGS FOR THE DOWNWARD-BENDING STANDING POSTURE.
0.50 N*M REQUESTS 90 DEGREES. THE MEASURED-BEND FEEDBACK COMPENSATES LOAD.
THE WORKING SIMULATOR USES 120 HZ PHYSICS AND 24/6 SOLVER ITERATIONS FOR
RESPONSIVE, NEAR-REAL-TIME GUI MOTION.
THE GUI RENDERS ONCE PER TWO PHYSICS STEPS (60 FPS TARGET), NOT AT 120 FPS.
THE TORQUE RAMP AND BEND COMPENSATOR ARE TUNED FOR A QUICKER RESPONSE.
PRESSURE-LIKE LIMB TUNING: HIGH STIFFNESS WITH MATCHED DAMPING FOR QUICK,
STURDY ACTUATION WITHOUT A LOOSE RUBBER-CHAIN EFFECT.
ACTIVE HIGH-PRESSURE-LIKE GAINS ARE ROLL 20,000,000/42,000 AND
YAW 30,000,000/51,000 (STIFFNESS/DAMPING).


WORKING - 12 DISC QUADRUPED - HEADLESS 90-DEGREE CHECK

FIRST KEEP THE +0.50 N*M QUADRUPED CONTROLLER RUNNING IN TERMINAL 1.
THEN RUN THIS IN TERMINAL 2:

cd ~/soft_world
. ~/ros2_humble/install/local_setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
SOFT_QUADRUPED_HEADLESS=1 SOFT_QUADRUPED_MAX_STEPS=1200 \
  ~/isaacsim/python.sh \
  install/soft_world/share/soft_world/scripts/soft_quadraped_grounded_working.py

THE FINAL_BEND LINES REPORT THE MEASURED ANGLE OF EACH LEG.
1200 STEPS EQUALS 10 SIMULATED SECONDS AT 120 HZ.


